<MessageLogging name="ML-Attribution" enabled="true">
  <DisplayName>LLM usage attribution to Cloud Logging</DisplayName>
  <!--
    This replaces a StatisticsCollector policy, which docs/21 section 4.4
    specified and which Apigee REJECTS in this org: "StatisticsCollector is
    not a supported policy" (bundle validation, 2026-09-14). Custom analytics
    dimensions are not available to us, so the authoritative usage meter
    described in docs/23 section 4.5 as mechanism A is Cloud Logging, not the
    Apigee analytics UI.

    METADATA ONLY, deliberately and permanently. No prompt text, no response
    text, no model output of any kind. docs/08's anti-pattern 3 and docs/09's
    GDPR purpose-limitation note both apply: this log is joinable to a named
    person via the department and app fields, so adding content here changes
    what the log legally is. Any such addition needs its own sign-off.

    department is logged; the user oid is not, for the same cardinality and
    data-minimisation reason it is a quota key but not an analytics dimension
    (docs/23 section 4.5). Per-user consumption detail lives in the apps' own
    BigQuery cost tables, which are access-controlled separately.

    The scan_* fields carry Model Armor's per-filter executionState. scan_* SUCCESS/NO_MATCH_FOUND means Model Armor answered and found
    nothing. It does NOT prove the content was inspected: an oversized prompt
    is SKIPPED per filter and still reports that way. See AM-ScanVerdict.xml.
    A value of "unset" means the flow variable did not resolve, i.e. the
    variable name in AM-ScanVerdict is wrong for this Apigee version and needs
    confirming in a debug session. Both are actionable; neither is a pass.
  -->
  <!--
    Token counts added 2026-09-15. Until then this log carried no usage figures
    at all, so the only record of consumption was the LLM token quota counter,
    which is not readable and which EV-TokenUsage.xml explains may never have
    been incrementing. Departmental usage reporting therefore depended entirely
    on each application self-reporting, with nothing to reconcile against.

    prompt and output are logged separately, not just the total, because they
    are billed at different rates (for gemini-3.5-flash, output is six times
    input). A single total cannot be converted back into a cost.

    Still metadata only: counts, not content. No prompt text, no response text.
    See the note above on why that boundary is deliberate and permanent.
  -->
  <CloudLogging>
    <LogName>projects/gclt-aicoe-dev-apigee/logs/llm-gateway-attribution</LogName>
    <Message contentType="application/json">{"apiproduct":"{apiproduct.name}","app":"{verifyapikey.VA-ApiKey.client_id}","department":"{llm_user_department}","proxy_path":"{proxy.pathsuffix}","status":"{message.status.code}","scan_prompt":"{ma_prompt_result}","scan_prompt_match":"{ma_prompt_match}","scan_response":"{ma_response_result}","scan_response_match":"{ma_response_match}","scan_prompt_failed":"{ma_prompt_failed}","scan_response_failed":"{ma_response_failed}","model":"{llm.model}","prompt_tokens":"{llm.prompt_tokens}","output_tokens":"{llm.candidates_tokens}","total_tokens":"{llm.total_tokens}"}</Message>
    <ResourceType>api</ResourceType>
  </CloudLogging>
</MessageLogging>
